\import{ftip-macros}
\meta{agent-authored}{true}
\title{Trace-quality intervention}
\tag{ftip}
\tag{evaluation}
\tag{harness}

\p{Long-horizon training needs two linked questions: which events must a
trace preserve, and how can a selector be tested without confusing
repeatability with coverage? The first question is answered by the trace
schema and behavior vocabulary; the second is answered by a fixed-budget
protocol.}

\p{The trace schema defines the record and its productive-persistence
distinctions. The fixed-budget protocol defines the comparison arms, state
interventions, metrics, and future-research gate.}

\transclude{ftip-00P2}
\transclude{ftip-00P3}

\p{With the trace schema and the fixed-budget protocol now in scope, the FTIP
boundary is operational: an admitted trace must preserve the declared decision,
evidence, verification, and recovery events, and every selector comparison must
report the finite run rates, held-out task and strategy coverage, and charged
selection/storage/restart costs defined in \ref{ftip-00P3}. A result may claim a
selection benefit only when its immutable arm, split, seed, and randomization
receipt supports that comparison.}
